ic mandate for rigorous safety standards.\n\nRetaining mechanistic interpretability ensures that we do not fall into the trap of 'many eyes' theory, which assumes that decentralized observers can catch failures that are fundamentally baked into the model's weights. If we treat AI as a public utility, the political coalition for this hybrid model would include both safety-conscious legislators and enterprise users seeking predictable, reliable performance. Historical precedent in aviation safety management supports this, where serious incidents are classified by the probability of occurrence rather than just observed outcomes, forcing companies to address latent structural risks before they manifest in catastrophe.",
